are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=-3$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/assets/3811fcaaf0bbf2158a046dca5c8dc232fd268bce664c810df9fe114a404296cf.png)\n\nNotice that $h(x)$ and $p(x)$ are continuous at $x=-3,$ while $f(x)$ and $q(x)$ both have a discontinuity at $x=-3,$ but they are *not* jump discontinuities." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/state.json" "file_sha256" "1173701a3cdf83ac4300d11b90214044dda01ea48bca1b8cbcc2fff4a826c8b5"} {"question" "q-104577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "34e8faa35fdb84b2df88f51d451b94aac251936d9b351dea5e31026c65f40fa0"} {"question" "q-104577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/state.json" "file_sha256" "1173701a3cdf83ac4300d11b90214044dda01ea48bca1b8cbcc2fff4a826c8b5"} {"question" "q-104577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/assets/131749caa4d5fd14d6cd58802b5e8bd6662c233f6a27f2317d491cbf3ab1f4d7.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/assets/3811fcaaf0bbf2158a046dca5c8dc232fd268bce664c810df9fe114a404296cf.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/assets/475ef6db32cd243d3f867f67c2a1feed2d64d087dff85d29cebac6cf10b2