\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo the second condition failed. It failed because the left and right-sided limits are not equal:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}f(x)=2,\\,\\,{lim}_{x\\to ,(-1)^{+}}f(x)=-1.\n$$\n\nThese limits both exist and are finite, yet they are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=-1$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\nIn the same way, the function has a jump discontinuity at $x=2.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have\n\n- $f(2)=-1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo the second condition failed. It failed because the left and right-sided limits are not equal:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)=1,\\,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)=-1.\n$$\n\nThese limits both exist and are finite, yet they are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=2$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\nNote that there is also a discontinuity at $x=4,$ but this is not a jump discontinuity." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/state.json" "file_sha256" "1173701a3cdf83ac4300d11b90214044dda01ea48bca1b8cbcc2fff4a826c8b5"} {"question" "q-104682" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "34e8faa35fdb84b2df88f51d451b94aac251936d9b351dea5e31026c65f40fa0"} {"question" "q-104682" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/state.json" "file_sha256" "1173701a3cdf83ac4300d11b90214044dda01ea48bca1b8cbcc2fff4a826c8b5"} {"question" "q-104682" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$x=-1$ and $x=2$ only"] ["text" "$x=-1$ and $x=4$ only"] ["text" "$x=-1$ only"] ["text" "$x=2$ and $x=4$ only"] ["text" "$x=2$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/state.json" "file_sha256" "1173701a3cdf83ac4300d11b90214044dda01ea48bca1b8cbcc2fff4a826c8b5"} {"question" "q-104682" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=-1$ and $x=2$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/state.json" "file_sha256" "1173701a3cdf83ac4300d11b90214044dda01ea48bca1b8cbcc2fff4a826c8b5"} {"question" "q-48119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/assets/f1e1a140e78362efddf48ba6744e2f88d109000fba8eae97818b024c2d249ad5.png)\n\nFor which points does the function $y=f(x)$ above have a jump discontinuity?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/state.json" "file_sha256" "1173701a3cdf83ac4300d11b90214044dda01ea48bca1b8cbcc2fff4a826c8b5"} {"question" "q-48119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function has a jump discontinuity at $x=-3.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have\n\n- $f(-3)=1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -3}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo the second condition failed. It failed because the left and right-sided limits are not equal:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{-}}f(x)=-1,\\,\\,{lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}f(x)=1.\n$$\n\nThese limits both exist and are finite, yet they are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=-3$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\nIn the same way, the function has a jump discontinuity at $x=1.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have\n\n- $f(1)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo the second condition failed. It failed because the left and right-sided limits are not equal:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)=-1,\\,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)=0.\n$$\n\nThese limits both exist and are finite, yet they are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=1$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\nNote that there is also a discontinuity at $x=0,$ but this is not a jump discontinuity." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/state.json" "file_sha256" "1173701a3cdf83ac4300d11b90214044dda01ea48bca1b8cbcc2fff4a826c8b5"} {"question" "q-48119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "34e8faa35fdb84b2df88f51d451b94aac251936d9b351dea5e31026c65f40fa0"} {"question" "q-48119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/state.json" "file_sha256" "1173701a3cdf83ac4300d11b90214044dda01ea48bca1b8cbcc2fff4a826c8b5"} {"question" "q-48119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$x=-3$  only"] ["text" "$x=-3$ and $x=1$ only"] ["text" "$x=-3$, $x=0$ and $x=1$"] ["text" "$x=0$ and $x=1$ only"] ["text" "$x=1$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040492/state.json" "file_sha256" "1173701a3cdf83ac4300d11b90214044dda01ea48bca1b8cbcc2fff4a826c8b5"} {"question" "q-48119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=-3$ and $x=1$ only"] "catego